<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the MemosNG app target.

  Every entry below was audited against the code that ships in this bundle, not assumed:

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp — PickedMedia.imported() reads
    `.contentModificationDateKey` off the copy it just made of a picked file
    (Packages/MemosFeatures/Sources/MemosFeatures/PickedMedia.swift). The copy lives in this
    app's own temporary directory, which is why the reason is C617.1 (timestamps of files inside
    the app container) and NOT DDA9.1: the timestamp is sent to the server as an upload's
    `last_modified`, and DDA9.1 forbids sending the value off-device.

  Audited and deliberately NOT declared:
    - UserDefaults: this app has none. There is no @AppStorage, no UserDefaults and no
      SceneStorage anywhere in the app or its packages; session state lives in the keychain and
      the outbox in the app group's SQLite store.
    - Disk space: nothing reads a volume-capacity resource key. OutboxRepository reads
      `.fileSizeKey`, which is a file attribute and not in the disk-space category.
    - System boot time: nothing calls `systemUptime` or `mach_absolute_time`.
    - Active keyboards: nothing calls `activeInputModes`.

  Nothing is collected: memo text and media go to the household memos-ng server the person
  running this app operates, and to nowhere else. There is no analytics SDK, no crash reporter
  and no advertising identifier, so NSPrivacyTracking is false and there are no tracking domains.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
